  "tvLegalSection1Title": "1. Nature of the application — a PLAYER only",
  "tvLegalSection1Body": "This application is a media PLAYER for playing audio/video streams supplied by the user. It DOES NOT PROVIDE, SELL, HOST, BROADCAST or INDEX ANY television channels, streams, audiovisual content, playlists (M3U) or portal credentials (Xtream). No content is included, preloaded or sold with the application.",
  "tvLegalSection2Title": "2. User-supplied content",
  "tvLegalSection2Body": "Users supply their own sources (M3U links / Xtream credentials), obtained from their own provider. Users are SOLELY responsible for content they add, play or broadcast, and for holding the necessary rights, licences and subscriptions.",
  "tvLegalSection3Title": "3. Subscription = SOFTWARE, not content",
  "tvLegalSection3Body": "Any payment or subscription pays ONLY for use of the application (the player and its features: interface, favourites, local recording, EPG…). It NEVER constitutes the purchase, sale, rental or provision of channels, streams or content.",
  "tvLegalSection4Title": "4. Lawful use",
  "tvLegalSection4Body": "Users agree to use the application in accordance with the laws of their country and not to use it to access illegal or copyright-infringing content. Unlawful use is strictly prohibited and is solely the user’s responsibility.",
  "tvLegalSection5Title": "5. Third-party content — no liability",
  "tvLegalSection5Body": "The publisher has no control over third-party content accessible through user-supplied sources and cannot be held responsible for it. It does not guarantee the availability, legality or quality of that content.",
  "tvLegalSection6Title": "6. Intellectual property and complaints",
  "tvLegalSection6Body": "All trademarks, logos and content belong to their respective owners. As the application hosts no content, copyright complaints must be addressed to the provider of the source concerned.",
  "tvLegalSection7Title": "7. Provided “as is”",
  "tvLegalSection7Body": "The application is provided “as is”, without any guarantee of continuous availability or absence of errors. The publisher may change or suspend some or all features.",
  "tvLegalSection8Title": "8. Personal data",
  "tvLegalSection8Body": "A technical device identifier is used for licence/trial management and support. Details: app.7themotion.com/privacy.",
  "tvLegalSection9Title": "9. Acceptance",
  "tvLegalSection9Body": "By installing or using this application, users acknowledge that they have read and accepted these terms. Full version online: app.7themotion.com/terms",
  "tvAudioWitnessHelp": "Test sound playing (10 s): voice, then noise. Same player as the channels. Muffled noise → device. Clear noise → channel.",
  "tvAudioNoReports": "No reports. Open a channel: the player records the codec, decoder and output. The spectrum is measured only when enabled.",
  "tvAudioOptionsHelp": "Spectrum: on the next channel, measures four points (decoder, clear voice, silence, AudioTrack) without changing the sound. FFmpeg: retries the software decoder; if it does not start within 8 s, the box takes over. Box AAC: on the next channel, AAC uses the box decoder (like ExoPlayer). If it fails, FFmpeg takes over this opening. Fallback: “per channel” (default) sends only the affected channel to the box after an FFmpeg failure; “whole session” is the previous behaviour, sending every channel to the box after one failure. Audio focus: “Zuno” (default) never reduces volume when another app or a beep requests audio; “Android” is the previous behaviour (volume drops to 20%). Outside app: “stop” (default) stops and releases audio when leaving the app, then reopens the channel on return; “pause” is the previous behaviour. Home: “native stop” (default) stops at onPause and nothing reopens outside the app; “legacy” waits for Flutter. Switch: “wait” (default) opens the next channel only after the previous AudioTrack is released, avoiding overlapping sound after many channel changes; “immediately” is the previous behaviour. Output: “stream rate” (default) uses the stream’s sample rate (44.1 kHz for many channels), with conversion by the box; “48 kHz” resamples in the app before output. Try it if sound is poor with a 44.1 kHz report. Test sound: 10 s of voice then noise, played by the same player. Enables measurement without changing the sound. Muffled noise → device. Clear noise → channel.",
